/*Q20. Write a Java program to print a diamond pattern of alphabets for a given number of rows using methods.
Class: alphabetDiamond
Implement the following static methods inside the alphabetDiamond class.
1. printRow(int row, int n)
• Accepts row (int), representing the current row number, and n (int), representing the number of rows in the upper half of the
diamond.
• Prints n - row leading spaces.
• Prints alphabets in increasing order from A up to the alphabet corresponding to the current row.
• Prints the remaining alphabets in decreasing order, excluding the repeated middle character.
• Moves to the next line after printing the row.
2. printDiamond(int n)
1. Accepts n (int), representing the number of rows in the upper half of the diamond.
2. Calls printRow() for rows 1 through n to print the upper half, including the middle row.
3. Calls printRow() for rows n − 1 down to 1 to print the lower half without repeating the middle row.
The alphabetDiamond class should read the integer n and call printDiamond(n) to display the complete pattern.
Input Format:
• Asingle line containing an integer n, representing the number of rows in the upper half of the diamond.
Output Format:
• Print the diamond pattern of alphabets as described above.
Sample Input:
4
Sample Output:
A
ABA
ABCBA
ABCDCBA
ABCBA
ABA
A*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class alphabetDiamond {
 
    static void printRow(int row, int n) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < n - row; i++) sb.append(' ');
        for (int i = 0; i < row; i++) sb.append((char) ('A' + i));        // A .. current
        for (int i = row - 2; i >= 0; i--) sb.append((char) ('A' + i));   // back down to A
        System.out.println(sb);
    }
 
    static void printDiamond(int n) {
        for (int r = 1; r <= n; r++) printRow(r, n);
        for (int r = n - 1; r >= 1; r--) printRow(r, n);
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        printDiamond(n);
        sc.close();
    }
}
